<Project>
  <!--
    CARD-0222: cap the growth of MSBuild's per-project "file writes" ledger.

    IncrementalClean reads $(IntermediateOutputPath)$(CleanFile), i.e. obj/.../(Project).csproj.FileListAbsolute.txt,
    the list of every file any previous build of this project wrote; filters it (FindUnderPath twice); and
    rewrites it, on EVERY build, and it only ever prunes entries under the CURRENT $(OutDir). Every
    OutputPath=bin-(name)/ build (the way delegates build while the daemons hold bin/) shares this one
    obj/ and appends its own output paths, which no later build ever removes; and before CARD-0110's
    bin-*/** exclude (2026-08-21) a bin-X build also swallowed every sibling bin-Y tree as content,
    recursively. Measured 2026-08-28: Antiphon.SessionRunner's ledger was 228 MB / 770,706 lines and
    Antiphon.Tests' 97 MB / 520,713 lines; a build of tests/Antiphon.Tests took 21m31s at near-zero CPU,
    of which ReadLinesFromFile + IncrementalClean on the Tests ledger alone was 157 s (181 s down to 13 s
    for the same build with the ledger reset). From the outside that is indistinguishable from a hung
    build (one dotnet process waiting, worker nodes idle), and it was the build half of CARD-0222's
    "did not reach the test phase" reports.

    This target runs before the SDK reads the ledger and deletes it when it is larger than
    $(AntiphonCleanFileMaxBytes) (2 MB; a healthy ledger is ~50 KB). The only thing lost is IncrementalClean's
    ability to delete orphaned outputs from EARLIER builds of this project in this OutDir, which is exactly
    the state every fresh clone is in. ReadAllText is the one size probe MSBuild property functions allow;
    on a healthy ledger it is a 50 KB read, on a bloated one it is still cheaper than one second of the
    ReadLinesFromFile it prevents.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <AntiphonCleanFileMaxBytes Condition="'$(AntiphonCleanFileMaxBytes)' == ''">2000000</AntiphonCleanFileMaxBytes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <Target Name="AntiphonResetBloatedFileWritesLedger"
          BeforeTargets="_CleanGetCurrentAndPriorFileWrites"
          Condition="'$(AntiphonCleanFileMaxBytes)' != '0' and Exists('$(IntermediateOutputPath)$(CleanFile)')">
    <PropertyGroup>
      <_AntiphonCleanFileChars>$([System.IO.File]::ReadAllText('$(IntermediateOutputPath)$(CleanFile)').Length)</_AntiphonCleanFileChars>
    </PropertyGroup>
    <Warning Condition="$(_AntiphonCleanFileChars) &gt; $(AntiphonCleanFileMaxBytes)"
             Text="CARD-0222: $(IntermediateOutputPath)$(CleanFile) is $(_AntiphonCleanFileChars) chars (limit $(AntiphonCleanFileMaxBytes)); deleting it so IncrementalClean does not spend minutes reading it. Set AntiphonCleanFileMaxBytes=0 to keep it." />
    <Delete Condition="$(_AntiphonCleanFileChars) &gt; $(AntiphonCleanFileMaxBytes)"
            Files="$(IntermediateOutputPath)$(CleanFile)" />
  </Target>
</Project>
